IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc12-order-65`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore) -- tests for Order 65 (roc12-order-65.l4).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the Rule (lines 7482 to 7530 of the source file) before the run.
-- Arguments are positional, in the order of each function's GIVEN block.

§ `O 65 r 1 -- application of the Order`
-- r 1(2).  Arguments: before a District Court; all parties filed their consent.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(2) this Order applies on the filing of the consent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a District Court case and all parties file their consent
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(2) this Order applies on the filing of the consent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a District Court case and a party has not filed: the "where" condition fails
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(2) this Order applies on the filing of the consent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a District Court case: the "where" condition fails
-- r 1(1).  Arguments: document kind that began the proceedings; the Order 6 Rule 5 answer; court level; consent filed.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `Originating claim` (JUST TRUE) `Magistrate's Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- limb (a): an originating claim before a Magistrate's Court
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `Originating claim` (JUST TRUE) `District Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- limb (b): a District Court case to which paragraph (2) applies
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `Originating claim` (JUST TRUE) `District Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "only": a District Court case without all consents is not within paragraph (2)
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `Originating claim` (JUST TRUE) `General Division` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "only" to Magistrate's Court or District Court proceedings
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `Originating application` (JUST TRUE) `Magistrate's Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "only" to proceedings begun by an originating claim
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `Originating claim` NOTHING `Magistrate's Court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- whether the document is an originating claim turns on Order 6 Rule 5, outside this Order
-- r 1(3).  Arguments: the answer of r 1(1); this Order provides otherwise for the matter.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(3) the other Orders continue to apply to the matter` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- this Order is silent on the matter, so the other Orders continue to apply
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(3) the other Orders continue to apply to the matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Except as otherwise provided in this Order"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(3) the other Orders continue to apply to the matter` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the paragraph speaks only of proceedings to which this Order applies
#ASSERT `o 65 r 1(3) the other Orders continue to apply to the matter` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- whether this Order applies is not answered

§ `O 65 r 2 -- upfront production`
-- r 2(1).  Arguments: the answer of r 1(1); list accompanies; copy accompanies.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(1) the pleading is accompanied as the Rule requires` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- list and copy both accompany the pleading
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(1) the pleading is accompanied as the Rule requires` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no copy: a bare "must be accompanied by"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(1) the pleading is accompanied as the Rule requires` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- no list
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(1) the pleading is accompanied as the Rule requires` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "in a matter to which this Order applies": the Order does not apply
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(1) the pleading is accompanied as the Rule requires` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- whether the Order applies is not answered
-- r 2(2).  Arguments: paper form; electronic format in a common format.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(2) the copy may be in this form` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- paper form
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(2) the copy may be in this form` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an electronic format in a common format the other party can use
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(2) the copy may be in this form` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a permission naming two forms does not forbid others
-- r 2(3).  Arguments: filed and served by a party; pleads an additional fact; refers to a new document.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(3) this Rule applies to the amended pleading` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) pleads an additional fact
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(3) this Rule applies to the amended pleading` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) refers to a document not referred to before
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(3) this Rule applies to the amended pleading` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- an amendment that does neither: "if" not met
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(3) this Rule applies to the amended pleading` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an amended pleading filed and served by a party: outside the scope
-- r 2(3) the exception.  Argument: the document was previously disclosed in the same proceedings.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(3) a previously disclosed document needs to be disclosed by reason only of the amendments` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "need not be disclosed by reason only of the amendments"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(3) a previously disclosed document needs to be disclosed by reason only of the amendments` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the exception speaks only of documents previously disclosed
-- r 2(4).  Arguments: the answer of r 1(1); produced in accordance with the Order; the Court ordered or permitted reliance.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(4) the party may rely on the document` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "must not ... rely on any document that was not produced in accordance with this Order"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(4) the party may rely on the document` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QA: "except as may otherwise be ordered or permitted by the Court" lifts the bar and grants nothing
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(4) the party may rely on the document` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a document produced as required: the bar does not speak to it
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(4) the party may rely on the document` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "In any case to which this Order applies": the Order does not apply
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(4) reliance on the document is barred` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the bar applies to an unproduced document
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(4) reliance on the document is barred` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the Court has ordered or permitted reliance: the bar is lifted
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(4) reliance on the document is barred` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- produced in accordance with the Order: not within the bar
#ASSERT `o 65 r 2(4) reliance on the document is barred` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- whether the Order applies is not answered

§ `O 65 r 3 -- excluded applications`
-- Arguments: the answer of r 1(1); the kind of application.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 3 the application may be made` (JUST TRUE) `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 9, Rule 17` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "no application under Order 9, Rule 17 or 19 or Order 11 may be made"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 3 the application may be made` (JUST TRUE) `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 9, Rule 19` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- likewise
#ASSERT `o 65 r 3 the application may be made` (JUST TRUE) `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 11` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- likewise
#ASSERT `o 65 r 3 the application may be made` (JUST TRUE) `o 65 r 3 any other application` EQUALS NOTHING -- the rule is silent on every other application
#ASSERT `o 65 r 3 the application may be made` (JUST FALSE) `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 11` EQUALS NOTHING -- "in any case to which this Order applies": the Order does not apply
#ASSERT `o 65 r 3 the application may be made` NOTHING `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 11` EQUALS NOTHING -- whether the Order applies is not answered

§ `O 65 r 4 -- simplified trial`
-- r 4(1).
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(1) the duty to direct that the case be set down for trial arises` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "If the Court is satisfied that the parties ... are unable to resolve their dispute without a trial"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(1) the duty to direct that the case be set down for trial arises` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the "If" is not met
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(1) the mode of trial is one the Rule names` `o 65 r 4(1)(a) a simplified trial under this Rule` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(1) the mode of trial is one the Rule names` `o 65 r 4(1)(b) a full trial to which the provisions of Order 15 apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(1) the mode of trial is one the Rule names` `o 65 r 4(1) another mode of trial` EQUALS NOTHING -- "such of the following as the Court deems fit" does not say that no other mode may be directed
-- r 4(2).  Arguments: the matter; the Court considers it relevant.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(2) the Court may have regard to the matter in deciding the mode of trial` `o 65 r 4(2)(a) the number of parties involved` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) is named
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(2) the Court may have regard to the matter in deciding the mode of trial` `o 65 r 4(2)(b) the complexity of the issues` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(2) the Court may have regard to the matter in deciding the mode of trial` `o 65 r 4(2)(c) the amount of the claim and the amount of the counterclaim, if any` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(2) the Court may have regard to the matter in deciding the mode of trial` `o 65 r 4(2)(d) whether the costs which may be incurred will be proportionate to the amount of the claim and the amount of the counterclaim, if any` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (d)
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(2) the Court may have regard to the matter in deciding the mode of trial` `o 65 r 4(2)(e) the nature of the action` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (e)
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(2) the Court may have regard to the matter in deciding the mode of trial` `o 65 r 4(2)(f) any other matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (f) "any other matter that the Court considers relevant"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(2) the Court may have regard to the matter in deciding the mode of trial` `o 65 r 4(2)(f) any other matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a matter the Court does not consider relevant is outside (f), which does not forbid it
-- r 4(3).  Argument: the stage.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time limit in minutes` `o 65 r 4(3)(a) the examination in chief of a witness` EQUALS 10 -- "(a) for the examination in chief of a witness — 10 minutes per witness"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time limit in minutes` `o 65 r 4(3)(b) the cross-examination of a witness` EQUALS 60 -- "(b) ... 60 minutes per witness"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time limit in minutes` `o 65 r 4(3)(c) the re-examination of a witness` EQUALS 10 -- "(c) ... 10 minutes per witness"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time limit in minutes` `o 65 r 4(3)(d) the closing submissions of a party` EQUALS 30 -- "(d) for closing submissions — 30 minutes per party"
-- Arguments: the stage; minutes taken; the limit as the Court extended it, if it did.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` `o 65 r 4(3)(a) the examination in chief of a witness` 10 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- exactly the limit
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` `o 65 r 4(3)(a) the examination in chief of a witness` 11 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE -- over the limit of 10 minutes
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` `o 65 r 4(3)(b) the cross-examination of a witness` 60 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- exactly 60
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` `o 65 r 4(3)(b) the cross-examination of a witness` 61 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE -- over 60
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` `o 65 r 4(3)(d) the closing submissions of a party` 31 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE -- over 30
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` `o 65 r 4(3)(c) the re-examination of a witness` 15 (JUST 20) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the Court extended the limit to 20 under paragraph (4)
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` `o 65 r 4(3)(c) the re-examination of a witness` 25 (JUST 20) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- over the extended limit
-- r 4(4).  Argument: the limit is one under paragraph (3).
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(4) the Court may extend the time limit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "any time limit under paragraph (3)"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(4) the Court may extend the time limit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- other time limits are outside the paragraph
-- r 4(5).  Arguments: the answer of r 1(1); judgment entered for damages to be assessed.
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(5) this Rule applies to the assessment of damages` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "where judgment has been entered for damages to be assessed"
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(5) this Rule applies to the assessment of damages` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the "where" condition is not met
#ASSERT `o 65 r 4(5) this Rule applies to the assessment of damages` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "In every case to which this Order applies": the Order does not apply

§ `O 65 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- No deadline is stated for these duties; each is run once with the act done.  #TRACE prints an outcome and no assertion line.
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 65 r 2(1) the duty of a party serving a pleading` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 65 a party serving a pleading` DOES `o 65 serve the list and the copy of the documents with the pleading` AT 1
-- expected: BREACH (the party relied on an unproduced document: a prohibition performed is a breach)
#TRACE `o 65 r 2(4) the prohibition on relying on a document not produced` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 65 a party in a case to which this Order applies` DOES `o 65 rely on a document not produced in accordance with this Order` AT 1
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 65 r 4(1) the Court's duty to direct the mode of trial` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 65 the Court` DOES `o 65 direct that the case be set down for trial` AT 1
